! ibox_supply.strap -- TWO I-BOX SUPPLY TIMINGS, 2026-11-17
! (docs/atlas_oracle.md, "Closing the residuals" item 13).
!
! 1. AN INDEXED IMMEDIATE VFL OPERAND COSTS ONE CLOCK OF INDEXING, NOT
!    TWO.  Perf. Char. Vol. 2 PDF 177-182 (printed 170-175) print the six
!    immediate compares at 3.61 us unindexed and 3.92 us indexed (12 and
!    13 clocks) at the preparation floor, where the direct pages pay the
!    full 0.6 us (K, PDF 127, I-BOX 3.61 against 4.22).  R23-9732 Figure
!    3.1.23 (PDF 87, printed 1-47/1-48) turns the word-boundary test on
!    only under "IMM-bar . VFL": an immediate skips it.  StretchTiming's
!    vflImmIndexedSaving (RECONSTRUCTION: the one clock is the pages'
!    difference).  Sixteen KI(BU,24) indexed by $X5 = 0 (E-box 10 + 1, under
!    the 13-clock decode).
!
! 2. AN FP LOOK-AHEAD LOAD'S OPERAND FETCH YIELDS TO THE INSTRUCTION
!    FETCH.  R23-9732 Figure 3.1.21 (PDF 85, printed 1-43/1-44): the FP
!    look-ahead load FPL2E is turned on under "NOT IC FETCH PRIORITY",
!    else "BLOCK TYPE 2 LD TO LA"; Blosk, TR00.722 printed p.30 (PDF 32,
!    read in the page image): "Since IC controls have priority, the IC
!    fetch is made ... The lookahead load cycle holds up its fetch during
!    this cycle".  StretchStorage's memCtl, for FP levels only (both
!    sources describe the FP load; VFL keeps Buchholz §14.3's order).
!    Twenty-four FP L(U) rotating over four consecutive words at
!    100011-100014 (octal), as the atlas's PDF 64 (printed 57) does; the
!    instructions are in the same four interleaved units, so the 1Y/2Y
!    refills meet the level fetches at the bus.
!
! RES gets the FP one the last L loaded.
!
! MEASURED, 2026-11-17 (CYCLES in run_tests.sh's run line).
!   the model as of this deck .......................... 398
!   OBSERVED INJECTIONS, each alone, each reverted from a saved copy
!   checked with cmp:
!   - vflImmIndexedSaving returning 0 (an indexed immediate pays
!     iboxCycles' full 2 clocks) .......................... FAIL cycles 414
!   - memCtl's fpYields forced False (an FP level keeps its place ahead
!     of 1Y/2Y) ........................................... FAIL cycles 413
!   Nothing else failed in either (PC and RES pass).  414 - 398 = 16, one
!   clock on each indexed KI.
! The controls: decks/prep_floor.strap (sixteen UNINDEXED KI, eight L
! from $X9, no memory operand) runs 349 under both injections, as
! without them (361 on batch27, 2026-11-18, also unchanged under both); decks/fp_internal_operand.strap (no VFL immediate, not
! run under the first) runs 208 under the second (its pin moved
! 208 -> 204 with the yield).

        SLC, (8)2000.0

START   LX, $X5, ZERO
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        KI(BU,24), 5($X5)
        L(U), FM0
        L(U), FM1
        L(U), FM2
        L(U), FM3
        L(U), FM0
        L(U), FM1
        L(U), FM2
        L(U), FM3
        L(U), FM0
        L(U), FM1
        L(U), FM2
        L(U), FM3
        L(U), FM0
        L(U), FM1
        L(U), FM2
        L(U), FM3
        L(U), FM0
        L(U), FM1
        L(U), FM2
        L(U), FM3
        L(U), FM0
        L(U), FM1
        L(U), FM2
        L(U), FM3
        ST(U), RES

PASS    BEW, $

        SLC, (8)2200.0

ZERO    DD(BU,64,8), 0
RES     DD(BU,64,8), 0

        SLC, (8)100011.0

FM0     DD(BU,64,8), (16)0028000000000000
FM1     DD(BU,64,8), (16)0028000000000000
FM2     DD(BU,64,8), (16)0028000000000000
FM3     DD(BU,64,8), (16)0028000000000000

        END, START
